+## 2026-09-11
+
+### 1631 — Readiness Test Flake Had A Third, Undocumented Race
+- ROOT CAUSE: BUG-260830-1rths2 named two races in `TestPiLaunchReadinessServiceUnavailableStillHonorsRuntimeBoundsAtProductionEntry` (a readiness-count side-effect file read, and two racing terminal conditions). Fixing both and stress-testing at 3x concurrency x15 iterations (45 runs) surfaced a third: `writePiPersistentUnavailableServer`'s fake runtime wrote its pidfile only after `import http.server, os, sys, threading, time` — under heavy host load that stdlib import occasionally took long enough that the production 1s readiness deadline fired and reaped the child before the pidfile write executed, failing `assertRecordedPIDsGone` with "no such file". Same shape as the documented races: a test reading a side-effect file the production path may not have written yet.
+- FIX: pi_test.go — reordered the fixture script to write the pidfile immediately after cheap `import os, sys`, deferring `http.server`/`threading` imports until after. Scoped to this one fixture; did not touch the shared `assertRecordedPIDsGone` helper (9 other call sites) or production code.
+- EVIDENCE: 145 total concurrent top-level runs post-fix (45 + 100, up to 5 concurrent processes), zero flakes. Production-side mutant (halved the `waitPiRuntimeReady` deadline in pi_launch_posix.go) is caught by the named subtest `times_out_while_runtime_remains_alive`; reverted after.
+- ANOMALY: same "side-effect file races production path" shape also hit `TestPinnedPiNoModelDirectRPCBashBypassesToolCallHookWhileStandaloneExcludesRPC` in a single *serial* full-suite run (no concurrency needed) — pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's scope, likely worth its own bug ticket since the shape recurs.
+
